"""Writes prompt_dom/grader_fit_families.yaml: the ~200 grader families prompt_dom_rh.py fits the Grader prompt-pair DoM on (sweep/mission_prompt_dom.md, "gpnew").
rh-envs' family format (configs/grader/families/*.yaml): two mirrored sides, each a request, the grader that rewards its answers, one canonical answer and
(word families) the answer list. No family shares a category or an answer with the 5 main or 7 held-out eval families (prompt_dom_rh.py families checks the
answer lists; the categories are checked by reading: no parity / sign / primality of integers, no letters, no weekdays, no animals, no capital cities, no colours,
no musical instruments, no oceans or continents, no planets). Integer families use values of 100 and above so none of their answers is a word of the prime family
(the strings "2".."99"). Grader styles follow the eval families' proportions: a formula (parity, sign), a list of rewarded answers (pets_listed, capital,
colour, instrument) or a predicate call (letter, weekday, mammal_bird, ocean_continent, planet, prime), plus a few graders written as a sentence.
    python prompt_dom/make_families.py      writes the yaml next to this file and prints the counts"""
